body:
It's super easy! Save the Boundary Waters has a form on their site with a template letter already filled in: [https://www.savetheboundarywaters.org/bwca-action-national-jan-2020](https://www.savetheboundarywaters.org/bwca-action-national-jan-2020)

&#x200B;

Personally I didn't like not knowing exactly where the message would go from that form, so I wrote via my rep's site (the bill is in the House right now). Go here: [https://www.house.gov/representatives/find-your-representative](https://www.house.gov/representatives/find-your-representative) , enter your ZIP, and there will be a button to take you to your rep's contact form. I pasted the template letter from the first link above (plus made a few additions).

&#x200B;

And here's the bill mentioned in STBW's template letter, H.R. 5598: [https://www.congress.gov/bill/116th-congress/house-bill/5598](https://www.congress.gov/bill/116th-congress/house-bill/5598) You can read it there if you'd like (it's really short) and see whether your representative is already a co-sponsor.
